# Occhio – The Big Hack 2026 build plan

Nov 14, 2026 · @vhs

## 1. Overview

We build **Occhio**, a camera app that tells blind people, by voice, what is around them, for the Mare Group FieldVision challenge. The same engine switches to an Industrial mode for aerospace and factory safety.

**The problem.** A white cane senses about 1 metre ahead, at ground level. It cannot warn about a bike coming fast, a person walking toward you, or a car backing out.

**The solution.** A phone or webcam watches the way ahead. AI detects and tracks objects, works out direction, distance and speed, and speaks only what matters: "Persona davanti, 3 metri", "Bici in arrivo da sinistra". When the image is bad it says "Guidance unreliable" instead of guessing.

**One engine, two markets.** Street mode helps visually impaired people. Industrial mode warns hangar and factory workers about vehicles and people. Only a profile (object list, distances, voice lines) changes.

### How Occhio covers the FieldVision brief

| Requirement from Mare Group | How Occhio does it |
| --- | --- |
| Detect moving objects and obstacles | YOLO11n on the Mac GPU (MPS) |
| Handle temporary occlusions | ByteTrack keeps IDs; memory of lost tracks for 1.5 s |
| Separate confirmed from uncertain detections | Confirmed = seen in 5+ frames with confidence above 0.6 |
| Timely spatial feedback | Voice and beeps with direction, distance, approach speed |
| Signal when guidance is unreliable | Reliability score from light, blur, confidence, blocked lens |
| Continuity, low latency, efficiency | Live FPS and latency counter; nano models; depth every 3rd frame |

### Why this can win

- **Usefulness:** helps a real person; anyone understands it in 5 seconds.
- **Relevance:** every requirement above is met and shown live.
- **Design and UX:** a calm voice that speaks only about danger, plus a clear screen.
- **Creativity:** "describe scene" with a vision LLM, two modes, a blindfolded test.
- **The sponsor:** Industrial mode speaks to Mare Group's own aerospace business.

