## 3. Architecture

Every frame goes through five stages: capture, detect, track, reason, speak. Only stage 4 (reason) is our own logic, and it is where we win.

&#91;embedded content: Occhio pipeline · 5 stages per frame\]

Detection and tracking are off-the-shelf; the Reason stage (confirmed vs uncertain, distance, approach, reliability, priority) is what the jury will judge.

### Tech stack

| Part | Tool | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Language | Python 3.11 | Team strength, all AI libs |
| Detection + tracking | Ultralytics YOLO11n + ByteTrack | Real-time on M5 GPU (`device="mps"`), tracking built in |
| Depth (distance) | Depth Anything V2 Small (Hugging Face `transformers`) | Metres from one camera; run every 3rd frame |
| Video I/O | OpenCV | Webcam, iPhone Continuity Camera, drawing overlays |
| Voice | macOS `say` (Italian voice Alice) in a background thread | Zero setup, offline, no lag |
| Beeps / stereo | `sounddevice` + `numpy` | Left/right ear, faster beeps when closer |
| Scene description | Claude or GPT vision API | "What's in front of me?" button |
| Voice commands (Tier 3) | `faster-whisper` small | "Occhio, cosa c'è intorno?" |
| UI | OpenCV window first; Streamlit dashboard optional | OpenCV is lowest latency for the live demo |

