```
Read CLAUDE.md. Implement detector.py: a Detector class wrapping ultralytics YOLO('yolo11n.pt') with model.track(frame, persist=True, tracker='bytetrack.yaml', device='mps', verbose=False), returning a list of Detection dataclasses (track_id, cls_name, conf, xyxy) filtered by the active profile's classes.

Then implement tracks.py: a TrackManager that keeps a Track per id with history of boxes (last 30), frames_seen, mean_conf, last_seen time and status in {uncertain, confirmed, hidden}. Rules: confirmed when frames_seen >= 5 and mean_conf >= 0.6; when a confirmed track disappears, mark it hidden and predict its box with constant velocity for up to 1.5 s, then delete it; if it comes back with the same id, it is confirmed again immediately. Thresholds come from config.

Then implement overlay.py to draw boxes: confirmed green, uncertain yellow, hidden grey dashed, with label '#id cls conf'. Show FPS and latency per stage (capture, detect, logic) in ms. Add pytest tests for TrackManager with fake detections, including an occlusion of 20 frames.
```

### Phase 2 – Understand and speak (Sat 14:00–17:00) · owner: Logic + Audio

- [ ] F5 Direction: left / ahead / right from the box centre (plus clock position, "a ore 2")
- [ ] F6 Distance in metres: Depth Anything V2 Small every 3rd frame, median depth inside the box; box-height fallback
- [ ] F7 Approach detection from distance change over the last 10 frames
- [ ] F8 Speed estimate and "fast" flag
- [ ] F9 Voice in Italian and English via `say`, in a background queue that never blocks
- [ ] F10 Priority: speak only the most dangerous confirmed object (closeness × approach speed × confidence)
- [ ] F11 Anti-spam: the same track and message at most once every 3 s; urgent messages interrupt
- [ ] F12 Reliability score (0–1) from brightness, blur (Laplacian variance), mean confidence and blocked lens; below 0.4 say the "unreliable" line and stop other warnings
- [ ] **Mentor checkpoint 1** around 16:00: show the live demo, ask what matters most to Mare Group

**Done when:** walking toward the camera triggers "Persona davanti, 2 metri", and covering the lens triggers the unreliable warning within 1 s.

```
Read CLAUDE.md. Implement depth.py: a DepthEstimator using transformers pipeline('depth-estimation', model='depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Small-hf', device='mps') running in a background thread on every 3rd frame; it exposes the latest depth map. Convert relative depth to approximate metres with a calibration constant we can set by standing at a known 2 m distance (add a --calibrate flag). Fallback when no depth: distance from box height using a known average height per class.

Implement spatial.py: for each confirmed track compute side (sinistra/davanti/destra by thirds of the frame width), clock position (10 to 2 o'clock), distance_m (median depth in the box), approach_speed_mps from a linear fit of distance over the last 10 frames, and time_to_collision_s when approaching.

Implement priority.py: danger_score = closeness * max(approach_speed, 0.1) * mean_conf, only for confirmed tracks within warn_distance_m. Return at most one message per cycle. Cooldown 3 s per (track, message type); 'danger' messages (distance < danger_distance_m or ttc < 2 s) skip the cooldown.

Implement reliability.py: score from brightness (mean gray), blur (variance of Laplacian), mean detection confidence, and a blocked-lens check (very low variance). Smooth with an exponential moving average. Below 0.4 => unreliable.

Implement speech.py: a Speaker with a queue and a worker thread calling subprocess 'say -v Alice' (Italian) or 'say -v Samantha' (English); urgent messages clear the queue and kill the current 'say' process. All texts come from the profile lines. Add pytest tests for spatial, priority and reliability.
```

